Package: sbwadjust
Title: Stable Balancing Weights for Covariate Adjustment in Trials
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Kayla", "Irish", , "kayla.a.irish@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Core routines behind "Simple Covariate Adjustment for Many
    Estimands Using Stable Balancing Weights" (Irish, Zubizarreta, Luedtke):
    fitting stable balancing weights (SBW) for a two-arm study by a
    closed-form solve with a nonnegative quadratic-programming fallback,
    inverse-probability weights as a comparison, and weighted Kaplan-Meier
    survival-ratio point estimates with bootstrap confidence intervals. A
    general-purpose covariate-adjustment interface is in development; the
    current functions expose the exact choices made in the paper.
